{"login":"rxlecky","id":35656626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjU2NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35656626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky","html_url":"https://github.com/rxlecky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T16:35:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T16:39:00Z","body":"Seeing that this issue seems platform/controller-dependent, I wanted to chip in with test results from Windows, using various Godot versions and controllers:\n\n| | Xbox One Controller| PS5 Controller|\n|--------|--------|--------|\n| Godot 3.6| Correct behaviour | Bug|\n| Godot 4.2.2| Correct behaviour |Bug| |\n| Godot 4.4.1| Correct behaviour | Correct behaviour | \n\nIt seems that the bug got fixed on Godot 4 somewhere between 4.2.2 and 4.4.1 and it only needs to be fixed on 3.x.\n\nAlso, the difference in behaviour between Xbox and PS controllers on Windows appears to be coming from the different underlying library being used for polling for events (XInput vs DInput).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867183788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.